  "notes": [
    "This shape covers ONLY the host mechanism (Component + its 11 FieldMappings + Repeater + its content Container, Type:\"Repeater\" — a seventh distinct Container Type value). Getting this right renders \"Repeater (N)\" with N live rows but every row BLANK.",
    "Making a row's template labels show actual per-row data is a SEPARATE mechanism layered inside Container_Sample02's own content tree: each bound label needs the Type:\"Variable\" + VariableRef(Type:\"DatasourceParameter\", Variable:\"item.<field>\") chain AND registration in the page's Page::VariableRef list — see variable_ref.json for that full chain rather than duplicating it here; the two shapes compose (host config here + N bound-label instances of variable_ref.json's pattern, one per visible field, inside this Container).",
    "selectedFields is written TWICE — once as a plain Array FieldMapping/Property, once again inline on Component.Data.selectedFields — both were present together on every live capture; write both rather than assuming either alone is read.",
    "view_id:\"admin\" is what a repeater needs to see ALL rows regardless of who created them (myitems/mytasks/participated/assigned are the narrower, user-scoped alternatives — same view-id vocabulary as the item data-plane's own admin routes).",
    "An on_click EventMapping on a per-row action Container inside here combined with kf.eventParameters.item (the clicked row's own data) is how \"click a row -> open its detail popup\" is built — see event_mapping.json's JSAction example, which is this exact pattern.",
    "Real ids typically use the manifest_id prefix only on a fresh single-widget add (e.g. `Button_<10-char-rand>`, `Metrics_<10-char-rand>`) — the scenario this template mints for — while built-up production pages (`all_pages_draft_20260806.json`) mostly carry the generic `Component_<rand>` id instead, and Repeater/Tab/MasterDetail/Breadcrumbs were never observed prefixed at all."
  ]
